-- title:
--   Diamond-equivariant modular description of a fibre of j
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be an algebraically closed field, $M$ a nonzero natural number with $(M:K)\neq 0$, $H\le(\mathbb Z/M)^{\times}$, $j_{0}\in K$, and $E_{0}$ an elliptic Weierstrass curve over $K$ with $j(E_{0})=j_{0}$. Let $F=$ `qExpFunctionFieldC K (CohCarrier.GammaH M H)`, the subfield of the Laurent series field over $K$ generated by the quotients $p_{f}/p_{g}$ of integral $q$-expansions of modular forms of equal weight for $\Gamma_{H}(M)$ (the image in $SL(2,\mathbb Z)$ of the preimage of $H$ under $\Gamma_{0}(M)\to(\mathbb Z/M)^{\times}$, $\gamma\mapsto d$), and let $x\in F$ have Laurent series the $q$-expansion `jqModC K` of $j$. Let $S$ be a finite set of places of $F$ over $K$ (valuation subrings containing $K$, proper, with principal ideals) consisting exactly of those $Q$ with $\operatorname{ord}_{Q}(x-j_{0})>0$, and let $\rho:\Gamma_{0}(M)\to\operatorname{Aut}_{K}(F)$ satisfy `IsDiamondPullbackModL`: for $\gamma\in\Gamma_{0}(M)$ and forms with $f_{1}=f\mid_{k}\gamma$, $g_{1}=g\mid_{k}\gamma$ and $p_{g}$ giving a nonzero series, $\rho(\gamma)$ sends the element with series $p_{f_{1}}/p_{g_{1}}$ to the one with series $p_{f}/p_{g}$. Then there is a map $f$ from the set of subsets of $E_{0}(K)$ of the form $\{u\cdot P: u\in H\cdot\{\pm1\}\}$, for $P$ of exact order $M$ (the unit $u$ acting through a natural lift of its residue), to places of $F$, such that: every $f(s)$ lies in $S$; every element of $S$ is some $f(s)$; $f(s)=f(s')$ holds precisely when some Weierstrass variable change $\gamma$ over $K$ with $\gamma\cdot E_{0}=E_{0}$ carries each $T\in s$, via `Point.vcInvFun`, to an element of $s'$; $\operatorname{ord}_{f(s)}(x-j_{0})$ equals the cardinality of the fibre of $f$ through $s$; and, for $\gamma\in\Gamma_{0}(M)$, if $s'$ is the image of $s$ under multiplication by (a natural lift of) the lower-right entry $\gamma_{1,1}$ modulo $M$, then $f(s')=\rho(\gamma)\cdot f(s)$, the automorphism acting on places by transport of valuation subrings.
--
--   This is the modular interpretation of the fibre of $j$ over $j_{0}$ on $X_{H}(M)$: the places above $j_{0}$ correspond to $\pm H$-orbits of points of exact order $M$ on $E_{0}$ modulo automorphisms of $E_{0}$, the ramification index at a place being the size of the corresponding orbit, together with the compatibility $\langle d\rangle[E_{0},\pm HP]=[E_{0},\pm HdP]$ for the diamond operators. It feeds the computation of inertia at the points of the special fibre used in the study of $X_{1}(p)$ and $X_{0}(p)$.
